{
  "text_input": "Patient was apparently normal 1 week ago when she complained of abdominal pain in the epigastric region & right lumbar region, insidious onset, gradually progressive, non-radiating, increased on supine position & eating spicy food; no relieving factors. Patient was taken to outside hospital for the same & USG (A+P) & UGI endoscopy was done for the same and diagnosed with H. pylori infection & cholelithiasis. Patient was referred to KIMS for the same.\nNo c/o fever \nNo c/o vomiting \nNo c/o loose stools \nNo c/o decreased urine output \nNo c/o burning micturition \nNo c/o bilateral lower limb swelling",
